  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 34,
    "summary": "Elihu teaches, God cannot be unjust, commit iniquity, pervert judgment, or respect persons—Man should bear chastisement and do iniquity no more.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Furthermore Elihu answered and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear my words, O ye wise men; and give ear unto me, ye that have knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "For the ear trieth words, as the mouth tasteth meat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Let us choose to us judgment: let us know among ourselves what is good.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "For Job hath said, I am righteous: and God hath taken away my judgment.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Should I lie against my right? my wound is incurable without transgression.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "What man is like Job, who drinketh up scorning like water?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Which goeth in company with the workers of iniquity, and walketh with wicked men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "For he hath said, It profiteth a man nothing that he should delight himself with God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore hearken unto me, ye men of understanding: far be it from God, that he should do wickedness; and from the Almighty, that he should commit iniquity.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 89
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 110
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 146
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "For the work of a man shall he render unto him, and cause every man to find according to his ways.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "2 Ne. 25:23; Alma 9:28; D&C 1:10; 6:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 92
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
