            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "If now thou hast understanding, hear this: hearken to the voice of my words.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Shall even he that hateth right govern? and wilt thou condemn him that is most just?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Is it fit to say to a king, Thou art wicked? and to princes, Ye are ungodly?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "How much less to him that accepteth not the persons of princes, nor regardeth the rich more than the poor? for they all are the work of his hands.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "In a moment shall they die, and the people shall be troubled at midnight, and pass away: and the mighty shall be taken away without hand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "For his eyes are upon the ways of man, and he seeth all his goings.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no darkness, nor shadow of death, where the workers of iniquity may hide themselves.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "Alma 12:14 (14–15); D&C 1:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "For he will not lay upon man more than right; that he should enter into judgment with God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall break in pieces mighty men without number, and set others in their stead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore he knoweth their works, and he overturneth them in the night, so that they are destroyed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "He striketh them as wicked men in the open sight of others;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Because they turned back from him, and would not consider any of his ways:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "So that they cause the cry of the poor to come unto him, and he heareth the cry of the afflicted.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "When he giveth quietness, who then can make trouble? and when he hideth his face, who then can behold him? whether it be done against a nation, or against a man only:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Silence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 75
          },
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 125
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Silence.",
            "prettyString": "TG Silence",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Silence",
                "entryId": "tg-silence",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "That the hypocrite reign not, lest the people be ensnared.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Surely it is meet to be said unto God, I have borne chastisement, I will not offend any more:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Chastening."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 64
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 65
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Chastening.",
            "prettyString": "TG Chastening",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Chastening",
                "entryId": "tg-chastening",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "That which I see not teach thou me: if I have done iniquity, I will do no more.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:32",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "Should it be according to thy mind? he will recompense it, whether thou refuse, or whether thou choose; and not I: therefore speak what thou knowest.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:33",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "Let men of understanding tell me, and let a wise man hearken unto me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:34",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "Job hath spoken without knowledge, and his words were without wisdom.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 35,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:35",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 35
      },
      {
        "text": "My desire is that Job may be tried unto the end because of his answers for wicked men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 36,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:36",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 36
      },
      {
        "text": "For he addeth rebellion unto his sin, he clappeth his hands among us, and multiplieth his words against God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 37,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 34:37",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 37
      }
